# Progress Log

## 2026-11-16 — Pinned, integrity-verified installer downloads (0.005/T002–T012, T013 partial)

- T002 decisions (recorded in the plan): FishDev files come from release-tag URLs and are checked against SHA-256 digests embedded per installer path. First release is `v0.5.0`. Third-party pins use a 7-day cooldown: uv 0.13.7, specify-cli 1.3.3 (PyPI wheel, digest-checked, installed from the local file), actions/checkout v7.0.1 and actions/setup-python v7.1.0 by commit SHA. uv `tool install` ignored a wrong `--hash` in a constraints file, so SpecKit's transitive dependencies stay unpinned (documented risk). uv's PowerShell installer does not check its archive (documented). uv 0.4.0 is the tested minimum. The installer now refuses existing installations instead of overwriting `progress.ai` and `handoff.ai`.
- Added the maintainer-only `.config/ai/tools/release.py` (`update`, `check`). `.config/ai/release.json` is the single pin record; the tool generates `.config/ai/release-manifest.json` and the marked blocks in `install.sh`, the README, the Windows guide, `fishdev-init.md`, and the CI workflow, repeating until output stops changing. It refuses to change published content under a release ID that already has a local tag. `fishdev.py` is unchanged.
- Rewrote `install.sh`: preflight, stage and verify all files, pinned uv and SpecKit, write, init. Supports `sha256sum` and `shasum`, stays compatible with bash 3.2, and has a `FISHDEV_SOURCE` test source (`https` or `file` only) plus a library mode for tests. The Windows guide stages and checks with `Get-FileHash`. The README bootstrap is download, check, run.
- Added rule SEC-001 (unpinned downloads) to FishDev's `rules.json`, a `release` step in FishDev's verification profile, pin review in `start.ai`'s monthly audit, `docs/release-integrity.md` (threat model, limits, update and release procedure), and `.gitattributes` LF pinning for digest-bearing files.
- Validation: `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` passed (33 tests, 22 new); the Python 3.11 suite passed; `fishdev.py verify` and Python 3.11 `verify --ci` passed; `bash -n install.sh` and `git diff --check` passed. An end-to-end install in an isolated HOME (FishDev files from a `file://` checkout, real uv 0.13.7 installer and SpecKit 1.3.3 wheel downloads) completed and produced the expected layout. `pwsh` is unavailable, so the PowerShell blocks are reviewed but not executed. T013 still needs a merge, the `v0.5.0` tag, an install from the published tag, and a hosted CI run with the new action pins.

## 2026-11-16 — Specification for pinned, integrity-verified installer downloads (0.005/T001)

- Created branch `specs/0.005-installer-download-integrity` from `main` and added `spec.md`, `plan.md`, and `tasks.md`. Addresses the mutable-download finding from the 2026-10-13 and 2026-11-12 monthly audits.
- Scope: FishDev workflow files (SHA-256 manifest, immutable release reference, stage-verify-write with no partial installs), the bootstrap (download-verify-run), uv and SpecKit (one recorded pin, same version on Bash and Windows), and CI actions (full commit SHAs). Maintenance: a deterministic manifest generator, a drift check in `verify`, an unpinned-download rule in `check`, and pin review in the monthly audit.
- Decisions: fail closed with no default bypass; document that digests from the same repository do not defend against repository or account compromise; release signing and adopter dependency pinning are out of scope. Source-reference, format, and version choices are deferred to T002.
- Scope: specification and planning only. No installer or runner code changed.

